    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        30,
        1830
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        620
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 - Text to Video (native stereo audio)\n\nGenerates video **with synchronized audio** (dialogue, SFX, music) from a single prompt, using the MiniMax H3 omni-modal video model (weights on the comfyui-models volume).\n\n**How to use**\n1. Write the prompt in the **MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo** node - describe shots, camera moves AND the audio (score, sound effects, dialogue) in one block. A short timeline breakdown like the default prompt works well.\n2. Pick the output size in the **Resolution Selector** (0.4 MP = fast preview, 864x480; 0.98 MP = native quality, 1344x768; the canvas caps at a 768x1344 area, keep multiple at 32).\n3. Set **Duration (seconds)** - the Math Expression node snaps it to the model's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps (max ~15 s).\n4. **Queue Prompt**. The MP4 is written by the SaveVideo node under `video/` in the output volume.\n\n**Turbo mode**: flip the **Turbo mode** boolean to true to switch in the turbo LoRA and drop from 20 steps to 8 (about 2.5x faster, slight quality trade-off). Default is quality mode (no LoRA, 20 steps).\n\n**Sigma shift**: the **ModelSamplingMiniMaxH3** node (video shift 12 / audio shift 3) is required - it gives the model its audio-aware sampling schedule. Do NOT swap it for a generic Model Sampling node (SD3 / AuraFlow / Flux): those strip the audio schedule and sampling crashes with 'ModelSamplingAdvanced' object has no attribute 'audio_scale'.\n\n**Image-to-video**: connect images to the first_frame / last_frame inputs of the MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo node.\n\nScripts: POST `workflows/minimax_h3_t2v_api.json` to https://<workspace>--comfyui.modal.run/prompt."
      ],
      "title": "Note: Usage"
    },
